**Given:**

First number = 21

Second number = 189

**Formula Used:**

Mean proportion between two numbers a and b is given by \sqrt{a × b}

**Calculation:**

Mean Proportion = sqrt{21 × 189}

⇒ Mean Proportion = sqrt{3969}

⇒ Mean Proportion = 63

**The mean proportion between 21 and 189 is 63.**
